I: This is the TLI interview TOPSY subject zero seven zero activity has been described. Here's your first photo. And your minute begins now.
S: It's a black and white photo of a male and a female. It seems to be an a little more old-fashioned photo. Maybe even a film poster. They both seem to be very I guess chiseled in a way. And both seem to be looking off in the distance. Has a very mischievous feel theme to it. Kind of reminds me of a film more or even just an old Bond film. They used a lot of contrast between the colors. A monochromatic scale. The male's eyes seem to be a little I guess diluted compared. The female looks a little worried in this case. In the background you also see a female as well.
I: So there's a minute. So you said the female looks worried.
S: Mhm.
I: What gave you that impression?
S: I think it's because she was trying to make eye contact with the male. And then she seems like she was trying to like cater to him. Like body language I guess.
I: Oh okay.
S: Mhm.
I: And then you said the the the picture had an overall feeling of mischievousness.
S: Mhm.
I: What gave you that?
S: I think it was a lot of the film noir kind of feel. Black and monochromatic black and white. And also just I think this was just like the style of the films that kind of were back in the day.
I: So perfect. Here's your second photo mhm and your minute begins now.
S: It looks like a scenic photo with something that looks to be the sun and a tower and a bridge. And people working below the bridge. They use a lot of lines, fine lines. Because there's also black and white. Use of monochromatic. Like the bottom corner reminds me of when Jean Vira was putting the workers to work. It's very difficult to see. There is no facial expressions. So I guess it's difficult to see. I guess what the people are feeling in this case. But by the overall theme of the photo I think it's us.
I: So there's your minute mhm.
S: I have no.
I: Follow up questions.
S: Thank you alright.
I: Here's your third photo. And german minute begins now.
S: There seems to be three people in the photo. One in the foreground and two in kind of the middle ground. There's a horse. It seems to be in a more rural area. Seems that woman to the right is has a child. And then the woman to the left is holding books. She seems kind of expressionless. Kind of I guess there's that solemn feel to it. The male in the middle. He seems to be working with the horse. This also is a black and white photo monochromatic scale. And the the feel of this whole picture is kind of more solemn and solitude. And yeah not as bright or happy.
I: There's your minute. So is there anything in particular about the photo that gave you that solemn feeling?
S: I think it was just the expression of the female in the foreground. Because I think because she's looking off into the distance. It seems like there's something more out there. And also with just all the characters. You can't really see their face. Or they're just not looking directly at you.
I: Perfect. Thank you very much.
